        "original_id": "0c825263-86bc-57d0-9baf-b9e6559dfd21",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Prince, Dresti\n- Groups: The Revolution\n- Works: “I Would Die 4 U”, Purple Rain, Space Cowboy cover of “I Would Die 4 U”\n- Topics: album singles, soundtrack sales, stage names\n\nFacts:\n- In 1984, Prince released Purple Rain as his sixth studio album, the first album to feature The Revolution, and the soundtrack to the 1984 film Purple Rain.\n- In 1984, Prince and The Revolution released “I Would Die 4 U” as the fourth US single from the album Purple Rain.\n- Purple Rain has sold over 25 million copies worldwide and is the third-best-selling soundtrack album of all time.\n- In 2002, Dresti changed his stage name to Space Cowboy and recorded a cover of Prince’s song “I Would Die 4 U”.",
